      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Seasonal variations (with a peak in winter and a fall in summer) in the level of arachidonic acid in low-density lipids, in heart rate, and blood pressures were studied in patients with angina pectoris. The findings are required for a better understanding the mechanism and for development of preventive measures against ischemic heart disease."},
